al Estate peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Hudson Pacific Properties, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $481M market cap on $831M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 56% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, thin -2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Insiders hold 2.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 2500% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 73% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 64/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.3M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hudson Pacific Properties (NYSE:HPP) Director Acquires $87,800.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/hudson-pacific-properties-nysehpp-director-acquires-87800-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794535743.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Hudson Pacific Properties (NYSE:HPP) Releases Quarterly Earnings Results, Beats Estimates By $1.01 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/hudson-pacific-properties-nysehpp-releases-quarterly-earnings-results-beats-estimates-by-1-01-eps.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794105660.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Hudson Pacific Properties (HPP) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/what-hudson-pacific-properties-hpp-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794100508.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope"